Subject: [PATCH] esp32/p4: enable every MIPI-CSI camera sensor driver for every P4 variant

cameraif's own micropython.cmake says the sdkconfig options are what matter
and that they live in the cameraif patch. Without them a P4 build ships
cameraif with an empty sensor-detect array, and cameraif reports "no camera
sensor answered on SCCB" on a perfectly good bus: esp_cam_sensor drivers
register through a linker section, so a driver that isn't compiled, or whose
probe the link dropped, simply isn't there.

Every MIPI-CSI driver esp_cam_sensor has is on, each with its MIPI
auto-detect and every mode, so whichever camera is plugged in is found and
named. The board names the CSI lanes and the SCCB pins, never the sensor.

A fragment on the P4 common config rather than on one variant, because the
CSI controller is a property of the chip, not of which radio is attached.

diff --git a/ports/esp32/boards/mpconfigboard_esp32p4_common.cmake b/ports/esp32/boards/mpconfigboard_esp32p4_common.cmake
index 876a186de..d61916f2a 100644
--- a/ports/esp32/boards/mpconfigboard_esp32p4_common.cmake
+++ b/ports/esp32/boards/mpconfigboard_esp32p4_common.cmake
@@ -3,4 +3,5 @@ set(IDF_TARGET esp32p4)
 set(SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS
     boards/sdkconfig.base
     boards/sdkconfig.p4
+    boards/sdkconfig.p4_camera
 )
diff --git a/ports/esp32/boards/sdkconfig.p4_camera b/ports/esp32/boards/sdkconfig.p4_camera
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..03d492a20
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ports/esp32/boards/sdkconfig.p4_camera
@@ -0,0 +1,209 @@
+# cameraif on the ESP32-P4: every MIPI-CSI sensor driver esp_cam_sensor has,
+# so any camera works on any P4 board. cameraif probes them in turn and opens
+# whichever answers.
+#
+# Each driver needs two options. Without CONFIG_CAMERA_<chip> the driver is
+# not compiled; without its AUTO_DETECT option esp_cam_sensor does not emit the
+# `-u` that keeps its probe against --gc-sections. Either one missing leaves
+# the probe out of the detect array, and cameraif then reports the camera as
+# absent with an SCCB error -- see cameraif/micropython.cmake, which explains
+# why adding the `-u` on the cameraif side instead does not work.
+#
+# Every mode each driver has is on too, so Camera(format=...) can open any of
+# them. Only the MIPI auto-detect: cameraif drives the CSI port.
+#
+# cameraif's sdkconfig.esp32p4 carries the same settings for builds made with
+# its build script, and its tests/check_sensor_configs.py keeps the two in step.
+
+# The OV5647 (the Waveshare boards' camera, the Raspberry Pi Camera (B) among
+# them): the windows (800x800, 800x640, 800x1280, RAW8 at 50 fps), 1920x1080
+# RAW10 at 30, and the whole sensor 2x2 binned, 1280x960 RAW10 at 45 -- the one
+# whose flip and mirror turn the same picture over, and the quietest in a dim
+# room.
+CONFIG_CAMERA_OV5647=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_OV5647_AUTO_DETECT_MIPI_INTERFACE_SENSOR=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_OV5647_MIPI_RAW8_800X800_50FPS=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_OV5647_MIPI_RAW8_800X640_50FPS=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_OV5647_MIPI_RAW8_800X1280_50FPS=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_OV5647_MIPI_RAW10_1920X1080_30FPS=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_OV5647_MIPI_RAW10_1280X960_BINNING_45FPS=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_OV5647_MIPI_DEFAULT_FMT_RAW8_800X800_50FPS=y
+
+# The Bayer sensors: cameraif streams these through the P4's ISP. The OV2710
+# is the ESP32-P4-EYE's.
+CONFIG_CAMERA_ARDUCAM_IMX500=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_ARDUCAM_IMX500_AUTO_DETECT_MIPI_INTERFACE_SENSOR=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_ARDUCAM_IMX500_MIPI_RAW10_1920X1080_30FPS=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_ARDUCAM_IMX500_MIPI_RAW10_1600X1200_30FPS=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_ARDUCAM_IMX500_MIPI_RAW10_1280X720_30FPS=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_ARDUCAM_IMX500_MIPI_RAW10_1024X600_30FPS=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_ARDUCAM_IMX500_MIPI_RAW10_640X480_30FPS=y
+
+CONFIG_CAMERA_GC2053=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_GC2053_AUTO_DETECT_MIPI_INTERFACE_SENSOR=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_GC2053_MIPI_RAW10_1920X1080_30FPS=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_GC2053_MIPI_RAW8_1920X1080_25FPS=y
+
+CONFIG_CAMERA_GC2607=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_GC2607_AUTO_DETECT_MIPI_INTERFACE_SENSOR=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_GC2607_MIPI_RAW10_1920X1080_25FPS=y
+
+CONFIG_CAMERA_GC4053=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_GC4053_AUTO_DETECT_MIPI_INTERFACE_SENSOR=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_GC4053_MIPI_RAW10_1440X1440_25FPS=y
+
+CONFIG_CAMERA_MIRA220=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_MIRA220_AUTO_DETECT_MIPI_INTERFACE_SENSOR=y
+CONFIG_CAMERA_MIRA220_MIPI_RAW8_1024X600_15FPS=y
